description:
Design a circuit that detects rising and falling edges on the input signal and generates a single clock pulse output for each detected edge. The module captures the transition of the input signal 'in' on the rising and falling edges, asserting the 'pulse' output high momentarily for each transition, while it remains low when there are no transitions. This edge detector ensures that a pulse is produced only at the moment of change in the input signal state, effectively acting as a pulse generator responsive to dynamic changes in the input.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input in,
  output reg pulse
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input in,
  output reg pulse
);reg prev_in;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (in && !prev_in) begin // rising edge detection
    pulse <= 1;
  end else if (!in && prev_in) begin // falling edge detection
    pulse <= 1;
  end else begin
    pulse <= 0;
  end
  prev_in <= in;
end

endmodule

